{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924313-2nd-ed-question-healing-other-vampires","id":924313,"title":"[2nd Ed Question] Healing Other Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-30T23:13:42-07:00","id":924313,"title":"[2nd Ed Question] Healing Other Vampires","content":"Hi! First off, new on the forums but not to the game. I've been GMing Mortal extensively for some time and have picked up VTR2 for an upcoming game I want to host.<br /> <br /> Problem is, I've been stumped by a question: How do you heal a vampire?<br /> First off, I'm well aware of how Vitae can be spent to heal off the damage on a vampire with different requirements for each damage type.<br /> But I'm referring to more along the lines of helping *another* vampire heal eg. First Aid.<br /> However, the books explicitly - as far as I've read - say that Medicine does jack to help a Kindred.<br /> <br /> I've taken the liberty of allowing one of my players who wish to specialize as a support player who helps his friends heal their wounds, by allowing them to speed up recovery if they took at least 3 dots with Kindred Physiology as a specialty. There are also the Night Doctor and a Coil which apparently speeds up healing, but beyond that: I was wondering if anyone here has figured out a good homebrew or canon solution where one Kindred helps another fix or heal their wounds?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12030-onerudeflowers","name":"OneRudeFlowers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12030_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T23:44:06-07:00","id":924321,"title":"","content":"Canonically, the closest you get is with Night Doctor, but healing is well within the wheelhouse for a Scale of the Dragon; probably Voivode or Ascendant. That being said, it doesn't really break the game immensely to give the Night Doctor effect as a general maneuver for the Medicine skill, if the character can justify it (with a specialty, as you suggest). Nor does Night Doctor have to be limited to Carthians -- many of the specialised Merits can be re-skinned to fit with other Covenants, or as more general merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T02:35:29-07:00","id":924368,"title":"","content":"Night doctor is the most I allow in my current game. A coil would be a good way to do it, though. You could either make a new scale or come up with an entirely new coil (a more recent one wouldn't necessarily go up to level 4 by the way) and matching scales. For the first option, the coil of the ascendant would be a good option, yes, like allowing medicine rolls to heal damage as long as the blush of life is active for the patient. For the second option, it could be a coil about boosting regeneration for the one practicing it, and allowing to repair damage to others to an extend with a scale. Knowing the usual scales, it would probably involve some pretty ulgy shit, though, but whatever works I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:31:07-07:00","id":924421,"title":"","content":"You could feed your vitae to them to heal them up. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T08:48:21-07:00","id":924477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924313-2nd-ed-question-healing-other-vampires?p=924421#post924421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could feed your vitae to them to heal them up. &gt;_&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I was going to suggest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:57:04-07:00","id":924718,"title":"","content":"The protection theme in blood sorcery lets you heal other vampires with spells. If they aren't a night doctor, then the best way for one vampire to act as the support is for them to have a large Herd and a good hunting roll, because the most efficient way to heal other vamps is to let them feed and heal themselves &quot;naturally&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T19:03:47-07:00","id":924721,"title":"","content":"Which fits nicely. It's how it always happens in the movies or books.<br /> <br /> Even in-game it can be an interesting trade-off. Do you risk ruining your relationship with another vampire by binding them with your own Vitae? Or your Humanity by sacrificing a human to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-01-2016, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T18:45:22-07:00","id":926202,"title":"","content":"Animalism, in particular the Undying Familiar devotion. They drain the animal and you still get to keep the ghoul as an undead familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","user":"PrinceRaven","date":". 07-04-2016, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:47:32-07:00","id":929823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924313-2nd-ed-question-healing-other-vampires?p=924421#post924421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could feed your vitae to them to heal them up. &gt;_&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Something a player of mine did for the Sheriff with memorable effects...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}